1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,910
On the night of the storm, nobody could see the summit.

2
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:04,390
Only white.

3
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:06,687
Only wind.

4
00:00:08,337 --> 00:00:10,707
Two weeks later, the search was called off.

5
00:00:11,377 --> 00:00:13,287
Helicopters can't fly that high.

6
00:00:13,957 --> 00:00:17,078
And in that weather, people don't survive.

7
00:00:18,728 --> 00:00:23,038
For the whole world, a climber named Ilyas was missing, presumed dead.

8
00:00:23,748 --> 00:00:25,612
But Ilyas was alive.

9
00:00:27,262 --> 00:00:28,532
And he had a number.

10
00:00:29,202 --> 00:00:30,072
Forty-four.

11
00:00:30,682 --> 00:00:36,189
Forty-four days until the weather window, when the winds would drop enough to try to get down alone.

12
00:00:37,839 --> 00:00:40,289
This is the story of those forty-four days.

13
00:00:41,079 --> 00:00:43,469
And of the one thing Ilyas got wrong.

14
00:00:53,519 --> 00:00:54,669
It came out of nowhere.

15
00:00:55,379 --> 00:00:58,729
One moment, the sky above the summit was clear and deep blue.

16
00:00:59,479 --> 00:01:02,307
The next, a wall of cloud swallowed the ridge.

17
00:01:03,957 --> 00:01:06,867
The wind hit at over a hundred kilometers an hour.

18
00:01:07,637 --> 00:01:09,247
Ice needles in the face.

19
00:01:09,937 --> 00:01:12,698
The rope ahead of him vanished into white.

20
00:01:14,348 --> 00:01:15,958
Ilyas did the only thing he could.

21
00:01:16,708 --> 00:01:20,218
He found a ledge below the ridge, dug in, and pitched a small tent.

22
00:01:20,888 --> 00:01:23,972
It was half torn before he even crawled inside.

23
00:01:25,622 --> 00:01:27,852
The ledge sat above eight thousand meters.

24
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:30,292
Climbers call it the death zone.

25
00:01:30,962 --> 00:01:34,572
The air holds only a third of the oxygen you breathe at sea level.

26
00:01:35,342 --> 00:01:36,652
Every breath burns.

27
00:01:37,322 --> 00:01:39,379
At night, it's minus forty.

28
00:01:41,029 --> 00:01:43,279
Far below, at base camp, his team waited.

29
00:01:44,029 --> 00:01:46,039
They called his name on the radio for days.

30
00:01:46,709 --> 00:01:48,052
Nobody answered.

31
00:01:49,702 --> 00:01:51,692
His radio had died on the first night.

32
00:01:52,542 --> 00:01:54,112
The cold had killed the battery.

33
00:01:54,902 --> 00:01:57,252
All he had left was a satellite tracker.

34
00:01:57,942 --> 00:01:59,532
And it could only do one thing.

35
00:02:00,242 --> 00:02:01,833
Count.

36
00:02:07,083 --> 00:02:09,393
Inside the tent, Ilyas took stock.

37
00:02:10,083 --> 00:02:11,793
A bag of freeze-dried food.

38
00:02:12,583 --> 00:02:14,793
One small gas canister for the stove.

39
00:02:15,483 --> 00:02:16,053
A knife.

40
00:02:16,763 --> 00:02:18,073
A plastic flask.

41
00:02:18,883 --> 00:02:22,048
And a sleeping bag, stiff with frost.

42
00:02:23,698 --> 00:02:24,888
He made two rules.

43
00:02:25,618 --> 00:02:31,868
Rule one: strict rationing.

44
00:02:32,678 --> 00:02:35,668
A handful of food and a few sips of warm water a day.

45
00:02:36,658 --> 00:02:36,851
Every minute the stove burned was fuel he would never get back.

46
00:02:38,501 --> 00:02:41,511
Rule two: never go outside after sunset.

47
00:02:42,321 --> 00:02:45,631
When the sun dropped behind the peaks, the temperature fell like a stone.

48
00:02:46,301 --> 00:02:50,261
Outside, at night, frostbite comes in minutes.

49
00:02:51,911 --> 00:02:55,681
To keep track of time, he scratched a line on the flask with his knife.

50
00:02:56,431 --> 00:02:58,562
One line for every day.

51
00:03:00,212 --> 00:03:00,742
One.

52
00:03:01,572 --> 00:03:02,142
Two.

53
00:03:02,792 --> 00:03:03,502
Seven.

54
00:03:04,152 --> 00:03:05,749
Twelve.

55
00:03:10,999 --> 00:03:12,609
The days became the same day.

56
00:03:13,279 --> 00:03:14,309
Melt snow.

57
00:03:14,979 --> 00:03:15,789
Eat a little.

58
00:03:16,599 --> 00:03:17,449
Sleep.

59
00:03:17,999 --> 00:03:19,741
Listen to the wind.

60
00:03:21,391 --> 00:03:23,301
Melting snow was the hardest part.

61
00:03:24,211 --> 00:03:26,941
A whole pot of snow gives you only a cup of water.

62
00:03:27,671 --> 00:03:29,854
And every cup costs gas.

63
00:03:31,504 --> 00:03:39,914
And the wind never stopped.

64
00:03:40,604 --> 00:03:40,802
It slammed the tent so hard, it felt like something outside was trying to tear it off the mountain.

65
00:03:42,452 --> 00:03:44,122
Sometimes he heard voices in it.

66
00:03:44,892 --> 00:03:45,622
His mother.

67
00:03:46,352 --> 00:03:49,222
His friends at base camp, calling his name.

68
00:03:49,892 --> 00:03:51,022
He knew they weren't real.

69
00:03:51,832 --> 00:03:54,723
That's what the death zone does to your mind.

70
00:03:56,373 --> 00:03:59,423
One night, he was certain someone was standing outside the tent.

71
00:04:00,173 --> 00:04:01,883
He could see a shadow on the fabric.

72
00:04:02,633 --> 00:04:04,483
He held his breath until sunrise.

73
00:04:05,133 --> 00:04:07,403
In the morning, there were no footprints in the snow.

74
00:04:08,033 --> 00:04:09,526
Only his own.

75
00:04:11,176 --> 00:04:13,946
By day thirty, his body was running on nothing.

76
00:04:14,716 --> 00:04:16,606
He was as thin as a skeleton.

77
00:04:17,276 --> 00:04:18,946
Every breath came with a rattle.

78
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:22,379
He couldn't feel his fingers anymore.

79
00:04:24,029 --> 00:04:25,619
But his mind stayed sharp.

80
00:04:26,209 --> 00:04:27,159
He kept counting.

81
00:04:27,869 --> 00:04:29,612
He kept the rules.

82
00:04:34,862 --> 00:04:36,492
Then came day forty-one.

83
00:04:37,362 --> 00:04:40,028
The worst storm since the first night.

84
00:04:41,678 --> 00:04:45,368
Around midnight, he heard the sound he had been dreading for weeks.

85
00:04:46,178 --> 00:04:47,928
A long, ripping tear.

86
00:04:48,658 --> 00:04:50,837
The windward wall split open.

87
00:04:52,487 --> 00:04:53,817
The blizzard poured in.

88
00:04:54,587 --> 00:04:56,237
Snow filled the sleeping bag.

89
00:04:56,947 --> 00:05:00,718
The temperature inside dropped to the temperature outside.

90
00:05:02,368 --> 00:05:03,438
He had to fix it.

91
00:05:04,328 --> 00:05:05,218
Right now.

92
00:05:05,968 --> 00:05:12,498
In total darkness, by touch, with fingers he couldn't feel, he pushed a needle through the frozen fabric.

93
00:05:13,248 --> 00:05:13,918
Again.

94
00:05:14,688 --> 00:05:16,357
And again.

95
00:05:18,007 --> 00:05:20,237
Every stitch could cost him a finger.

96
00:05:20,967 --> 00:05:21,717
He knew that.

97
00:05:22,427 --> 00:05:23,962
He kept sewing.

98
00:05:25,612 --> 00:05:28,142
By dawn, the hole was closed.

99
00:05:28,812 --> 00:05:29,902
The tent held.

100
00:05:30,612 --> 00:05:33,657
He had survived the night that should have killed him.

101
00:05:35,307 --> 00:05:37,277
His hands were burning with pain.

102
00:05:38,007 --> 00:05:39,277
And that was good news.

103
00:05:40,007 --> 00:05:43,073
Pain meant they were still alive.

104
00:05:48,323 --> 00:05:50,473
Three days later, he scratched the last line.

105
00:05:51,183 --> 00:05:53,117
Forty-four.

106
00:05:54,767 --> 00:05:56,237
The storm had stopped.

107
00:05:56,967 --> 00:05:59,897
For the first time in six weeks, there was no wind.

108
00:06:00,627 --> 00:06:03,740
Only a ringing, total silence.

109
00:06:05,390 --> 00:06:07,800
He counted the lines on the flask one more time.

110
00:06:08,390 --> 00:06:09,240
Forty-four.

111
00:06:09,930 --> 00:06:13,853
For the first time in six weeks, he let himself smile.

112
00:06:15,503 --> 00:06:19,554
Ilyas cut the frozen zipper with his knife, and looked outside.

113
00:06:21,204 --> 00:06:24,474
The first rays of sun were painting the Himalayas blood red.

114
00:06:25,264 --> 00:06:28,074
An endless ocean of white peaks below him.

115
00:06:28,784 --> 00:06:29,534
He had made it.

116
00:06:30,364 --> 00:06:32,254
Forty-four days in the death zone.

117
00:06:33,004 --> 00:06:34,357
Alive.

118
00:06:39,607 --> 00:06:40,937
Then he looked at the tracker.

119
00:06:41,647 --> 00:06:43,457
He had stopped checking it weeks ago.

120
00:06:44,167 --> 00:06:46,027
He trusted his flask.

121
00:06:47,677 --> 00:06:50,242
The screen said: day fifty-two.

122
00:06:51,892 --> 00:06:52,862
Fifty-two.

123
00:06:53,432 --> 00:06:54,921
Not forty-four.

124
00:06:56,571 --> 00:06:58,761
In the thin air, he had been passing out.

125
00:06:59,491 --> 00:07:00,561
For hours.

126
00:07:01,171 --> 00:07:02,981
Sometimes for whole days.

127
00:07:03,691 --> 00:07:07,356
And on those days, nobody scratched a line on the flask.

128
00:07:09,006 --> 00:07:11,316
Which meant the weather window wasn't about to open.

129
00:07:12,266 --> 00:07:13,616
It had already been open.

130
00:07:14,406 --> 00:07:15,656
For eight days.

131
00:07:16,426 --> 00:07:18,165
And it was closing.

132
00:07:19,815 --> 00:07:22,985
On the horizon, a grey wall of cloud was already rising.

133
00:07:23,575 --> 00:07:24,565
The next storm.

134
00:07:25,255 --> 00:07:27,024
Maybe a bigger one.

135
00:07:28,674 --> 00:07:32,824
Below him lay three thousand meters of ice, cliffs and crevasses.

136
00:07:33,694 --> 00:07:35,511
And he could barely stand.

137
00:07:37,161 --> 00:07:38,091
The food.

138
00:07:38,761 --> 00:07:39,611
The gas.

139
00:07:40,341 --> 00:07:41,111
His strength.

140
00:07:41,841 --> 00:07:43,611
Almost everything was gone.

141
00:07:44,281 --> 00:07:46,051
He had maybe one day left in him.

142
00:07:46,641 --> 00:07:48,364
Maybe less.

143
00:07:50,014 --> 00:07:52,764
Ilyas survived forty-four days at the top of the world.

144
00:07:53,414 --> 00:07:54,324
Or fifty-two.

145
00:07:55,054 --> 00:07:57,408
But the hardest part was still ahead.

146
00:07:59,058 --> 00:07:59,808
Getting down.

147
00:08:00,498 --> 00:08:01,763
Alive.

148
00:08:03,413 --> 00:08:04,563
Could you have survived?

149
00:08:05,313 --> 00:08:07,743
Tell me in the comments how many days you would last.

150
00:08:08,553 --> 00:08:11,263
And if you want to see what happened on the way down, subscribe.

151
00:08:11,933 --> 00:08:13,501
The descent is coming.
